{"id": "unknown-2026-05-20-009", "date": "2026-05-20", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 5, "week": 21, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["expand"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "EU seeks more transparent, biz-friendly Bangladesh trade environment", "content": "The EU has expressed keen interest in further expanding trade and investment cooperation with Bangladesh, calling for a more transparent and business-friendly trading environment in the latter. \nThe interest was conveyed by EU ambassador to Bangladesh Michael Miller to Bangladesh Commerce Minister Khandakar Abdul Muktadir. \nThey discussed reducing non-tariff barriers and simplifying exim procedures. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/eu-seeks-more-transparent-biz-friendly-bangladesh-trade-environment-310421-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-05-20-010", "date": "2026-05-20", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 5, "week": 21, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["cotton_price"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": -0.17, "keywords": ["improve", "weak", "pressure"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "ICE cotton weakens on US dollar strength, improved rain hopes", "content": "ICE cotton weakened as a stronger US dollar, soft export enquiry, favourable US planting weather and rising certified stocks pressured sentiment.\nJuly 2026 settled at 82.33 cents, down 3.6 per cent.\nPlanting reached 41 per cent, slightly above last year, while cautious mill buying, weak China textile demand and lower commodity markets kept the short-term tone bearish.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/ice-cotton-weakens-on-us-dollar-strength-improved-rain-hopes-310420-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-05-20-011", "date": "2026-05-20", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 5, "week": 21, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": []}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Vietnam to set up government trade negotiation delegation", "content": "Vietnam will set up a government delegation for international economic and trade negotiations.\nThe minister of industry and trade will head the delegation.\nThe delegation will assist the PM in directing ministries, sectors and localities in negotiations, signing, coordination of ratification and approval, as well as implementation of international treaties and agreements on economic and trade matters.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/vietnam-to-set-up-government-trade-negotiation-delegation-310412-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-05-20-012", "date": "2026-05-20", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 5, "week": 21, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["cotton_price", "supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "neutral", "score": 0.0, "keywords": ["record", "slow", "weak"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "South India cotton yarn stable as weak demand offsets export support", "content": "Cotton yarn prices in South India remained largely stable, with Tiruppur recording marginal gains while Mumbai and Gujarat stayed steady.\nWeak domestic demand, truck shortages linked to mango transportation, and labour constraints slowed trade and downstream consumption.\nHowever, strong export demand, higher cotton costs and spinning mills’ bullish sentiment continued to support the market.", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/south-india-cotton-yarn-stable-as-weak-demand-offsets-export-support-310410-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
{"id": "unknown-2026-05-20-013", "date": "2026-05-20", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q2", "month": 5, "week": 21, "weekday": "Wed"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift"], "sentiment": {"label": "negative", "score": -0.5, "keywords": ["slow"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.5, "reasons": []}, "title": "Bangladesh garment sector distant from renewable energy target: Study", "content": "Bangladesh garment units are quite far from meeting clean energy consumption targets due to high renewable energy costs, limited rooftop space, and policy bottlenecks that are slowing adoption across the sector, a study revealed. \nEighty-eight per cent of respondents cited high installation costs as a barrier to renewable energy adoption, while 42 per cent pointed to high maintenance costs. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_apparel", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/apparel-news/bangladesh-garment-sector-distant-from-renewable-energy-target-study-310422-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
